WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:02.970
OPENING

00:10.110 --> 00:11.500
Joe...

00:15.210 --> 00:19.170
I don't really like guys who talk too much.

00:20.080 --> 00:24.190
Jin... You're not serious, are you?

00:24.190 --> 00:29.180
You've done a good job so far.
But you've already served your purpose.

00:40.900 --> 00:43.740
This is goodbye, Joe.

00:46.750 --> 01:00.120
Sora ni toketa hane o matoi tobitate tsubasa de

00:46.750 --> 00:53.360
Cloaked in feathers melted into the sky

00:53.360 --> 01:00.130
Take flight on wings

01:14.470 --> 01:17.640
Morokute nigai kajitsu no you ni

01:14.480 --> 01:17.650
Like fragile but bitter fruit

01:17.640 --> 01:20.850
Hito no kokoro o miryou suru no

01:17.650 --> 01:20.860
It fascinates people's hearts

01:20.850 --> 01:23.950
Togi sumasareta shiroi yubi de

01:20.860 --> 01:22.360
The shadow that manipulates

01:22.360 --> 01:23.960
With sharpened fingers gleaming white

01:23.950 --> 01:27.120
Ayatsuru kage wa chi no kaori

01:23.960 --> 01:27.130
Smells of blood

01:27.120 --> 01:40.120
Shizumi aseta kodou o yobi samasu shi no sasayaki

01:27.130 --> 01:33.570
The whisper of Death

01:33.570 --> 01:40.130
That awakens fading heartbeats

01:41.100 --> 01:47.470
Sora ni toketa hane o matoi

01:41.110 --> 01:47.480
Cloaked in feathers melted into the sky

01:47.470 --> 01:53.710
Tobitatsu no wa gin no tsubasa

01:47.480 --> 01:53.720
Silver wings take flight

01:53.710 --> 02:00.190
Fukai kaze ni tsume o tatete

01:53.720 --> 02:00.190
Become the power that tears at deep winds

02:00.190 --> 02:09.920
Kirisaku chikara to nare

02:00.190 --> 02:09.930
With poised claws

02:10.910 --> 02:14.100
Brought to you by
BiG-GuY Fansubbing

02:17.700 --> 02:22.280
Episode 9
Aid

02:49.600 --> 02:51.330
Counterattack with the Gladiators!

02:55.700 --> 02:57.470
Steve, move out!

03:00.240 --> 03:01.640
Got it.

03:10.490 --> 03:11.920
Shiba.

03:12.220 --> 03:14.590
Oh, it's you.

03:14.590 --> 03:16.560
What's the big hurry?

03:16.560 --> 03:19.550
Deploying the Gladiators, are you?

03:20.900 --> 03:23.330
Sorry, but I'm in a bit of a hurry.

03:23.330 --> 03:28.360
But if you wanna fight me face to face without
relying on that thing, then I'll take you on.

03:39.010 --> 03:40.540
The Gladiator!

03:40.920 --> 03:43.150
So there was a bomb on the
transport helicopter, too?

03:47.160 --> 03:48.250
Gas!

03:48.690 --> 03:50.390
Get Venus out of here!

04:19.720 --> 04:20.650
Joe!

04:29.700 --> 04:30.790
Jin...

04:36.900 --> 04:38.000
Renée!

04:51.820 --> 04:54.410
To... ra... ji...

04:57.730 --> 05:00.320
She's our hostage. Take her away.

05:01.560 --> 05:06.330
Fool. You should've escaped earlier, but no, you had to be loyal.

05:26.250 --> 05:26.690
Sickbay

05:32.130 --> 05:34.700
Why are we stuck on this same screen?

05:34.700 --> 05:37.200
What's going on with Satsuma?

05:37.200 --> 05:39.530
Can't help it, Boss.

05:39.530 --> 05:42.600
The news is still being censored.

05:42.600 --> 05:44.110
In all this confusion,

05:44.110 --> 05:49.010
I wouldn't be surprised if the damn military
schemed to have Buichi arrested on false charges.

05:49.440 --> 05:53.380
Captain, Joe Katsuragi's surgery
has been completed.

05:53.380 --> 05:56.650
The medical officer would like to have
a word with you later.

05:56.650 --> 05:59.350
No, that's okay. I'll go see him.

06:04.090 --> 06:07.080
I see. I understand. Thank you for everything.

06:14.370 --> 06:18.110
Oh? So even you worry about others, huh?

06:18.110 --> 06:20.540
Who knew you had such admirable qualities?

06:20.540 --> 06:22.010
Whatever...

06:22.210 --> 06:26.380
But don't worry about him.
He's not one to die easily.

06:26.380 --> 06:29.280
Who said I was worried?!

06:29.580 --> 06:34.490
Well, if you ask me, she's the one
I really worry about.

06:39.660 --> 06:41.290
You have to eat.

06:49.500 --> 06:51.410
From Buichi?

06:51.410 --> 06:53.340
You sure it's not some kind of mistake?

06:53.340 --> 06:58.780
No mistake. The code pattern used
is known only by Satsuma and us.

06:58.780 --> 07:01.550
Early dawn this morning.
Escape from Satsuma. A success.

07:01.550 --> 07:03.350
Chief injured.

07:03.480 --> 07:06.190
Injured? What's the extent?

07:06.190 --> 07:09.660
That's all the information that was sent.

07:09.660 --> 07:13.060
That means we don't know where
he's headed, either?

07:13.390 --> 07:15.520
I know where he's going.

07:15.830 --> 07:19.820
We had decided long ago on where to go
in case of an emergency.

07:21.040 --> 07:23.060
We're heading to Tanegashima!

07:37.750 --> 07:39.950
There are no problems with the central system.

07:39.950 --> 07:43.420
We will expedite repair work and
make conversions on the armor.

07:43.420 --> 07:44.990
Okay.

07:44.990 --> 07:47.460
If only you would tell us everything,

07:47.460 --> 07:52.200
then we wouldn't even worry about
a little damage to the Gladiator.

07:52.700 --> 07:56.770
I'll give you more information
once we get Sana back.

07:56.770 --> 07:58.770
I'm sure if you were in my shoes,

07:58.770 --> 08:03.180
you wouldn't be foolish enough to put all your
cards on the table at once either, right?

08:04.310 --> 08:07.580
What do you think Drake's up to?

08:08.250 --> 08:10.650
Is he planning on bringing Jin over to our side?

08:11.020 --> 08:12.420
Who knows...

08:12.420 --> 08:17.020
So Renée got the boot too?
Boy, she sure messed up.

08:17.730 --> 08:19.830
The Moon again.

08:19.830 --> 08:21.350
Moon?

08:21.700 --> 08:24.000
I'm telling your fortune.

08:24.000 --> 08:26.730
Have you forgotten what this means?

08:37.180 --> 08:38.710
What's the matter?

08:38.710 --> 08:41.770
I'm not so stupid as to fight you face to face.

08:49.790 --> 08:51.850
"Betrayal..."

08:54.260 --> 08:57.600
Looks like that rings a bell for you.

09:17.990 --> 09:19.420
Did you eat?

09:20.620 --> 09:22.220
What is it?

09:22.220 --> 09:25.030
What could the captain possibly
want with a prisoner?

09:25.030 --> 09:27.760
Well, I'm just killing time.

09:27.760 --> 09:30.060
It's a long trip to Tanegashima.

09:30.730 --> 09:32.360
Tanegashima?

09:32.600 --> 09:34.860
I don't care if you tell Phantom, you know.

09:35.240 --> 09:36.970
Are you being sarcastic?

09:37.740 --> 09:42.640
I'm sure you know that's not the kind of place I can
ever go back to after committing such a blunder.

09:43.840 --> 09:47.340
I'm surprised you've stayed
at a place like that this long.

09:50.420 --> 09:57.630
Phantom is actually quite a comfortable place
to those who have nothing to believe in.

09:57.630 --> 10:01.320
Because it's a group of people
that doesn't trust anybody.

10:02.230 --> 10:06.720
And yet I trusted them, even if it was for
a short time. I was such an idiot.

10:09.300 --> 10:11.340
You sure sound bitter.

10:11.340 --> 10:16.170
So if I had asked you to come with me
back then, you would have?

10:18.980 --> 10:23.920
If there's nowhere for you to go,
you're welcome to stay here.

10:24.420 --> 10:26.120
As a prisoner?

10:26.120 --> 10:29.890
How you'll be treated will
all depend on how you act.

10:30.690 --> 10:32.630
What do you mean?

10:34.260 --> 10:36.250
What the hell do you mean?

10:38.370 --> 10:40.770
Classified information has been leaked?

10:41.170 --> 10:42.370
You sure about that?

10:42.370 --> 10:46.910
Yes. We discovered it while looking
into Satsuma's falsehoods.

10:46.910 --> 10:50.570
There is definitely something
suspicious about Drake's activities.

10:51.910 --> 10:55.250
I see... If that's true then things
will get interesting...

10:56.380 --> 10:58.250
Look into it.

10:58.250 --> 10:59.840
Yes, sir.

11:01.420 --> 11:02.590
What is it?

11:02.590 --> 11:05.790
An anti-submarine patrol plane
belonging to the 10th Division

11:05.790 --> 11:10.430
reports that a submarine appearing to be
the Ishin has been located.

11:10.430 --> 11:11.570
What?

11:11.570 --> 11:16.170
Lts fleets are currently cruising the area.

11:16.170 --> 11:18.010
Have them rush to the scene immediately!

11:18.010 --> 11:21.180
Upon confirmation, switch to Attack Mode!

11:21.180 --> 11:21.940
Yes, sir.

11:26.080 --> 11:29.110
Looks like the tides are turning.

11:31.520 --> 11:34.010
There's a fleet headed in our direction?

11:35.460 --> 11:38.890
From the way it's moving, it knows we're here.

11:39.030 --> 11:42.690
Looks like there's gonna be trouble...

11:44.630 --> 11:46.860
Why did you put him here?

11:47.570 --> 11:50.970
Structure-wise, this is the safest place to be.

11:52.240 --> 11:54.940
Are we going into battle again?

11:54.940 --> 11:56.840
Sana, take care of him, okay?

11:59.550 --> 12:01.540
Jeez, gimme a break!

12:16.260 --> 12:17.420
You want some?

12:20.030 --> 12:22.530
Man, what's up with you?!

12:24.540 --> 12:26.740
Crap, it's starting!

12:26.740 --> 12:28.970
I can't see anything from here!

12:35.120 --> 12:38.110
I'll protect you at all costs, Sana!

12:38.520 --> 12:39.720
Jin...

12:39.720 --> 12:42.850
Jin... Why?

12:52.200 --> 12:53.960
Let's get out of here, Joe.

13:24.400 --> 13:25.590
Sana...

13:37.910 --> 13:41.580
Direct hit on enemy cruiser Shiranui!

13:41.720 --> 13:43.020
Good job!

13:43.020 --> 13:47.820
Next, open tubes 3 and 4! Harpoon stand-by!

14:01.770 --> 14:04.260
Damn, they're going all out.

14:05.470 --> 14:10.030
Surrounded by this much material superiority,
even the Ishin won't be able to...

14:10.880 --> 14:13.450
Does the military know that Sana's on board?

14:13.450 --> 14:18.190
Katsura doesn't know.
But it would be useless to tell him.

14:18.190 --> 14:20.480
He doesn't trust Phantom.

14:20.860 --> 14:22.450
But...

14:23.790 --> 14:26.160
They just keep doing things to get in the way.

14:26.160 --> 14:28.420
Looks like I have no choice but to crush them.

14:41.850 --> 14:42.810
NUMBER6
BULKHEAD

14:43.340 --> 14:44.950
We're taking on water?

14:44.950 --> 14:46.740
Can't the ship take it?

14:47.310 --> 14:50.380
No way. Water's coming in from too many areas.

14:50.380 --> 14:53.410
It exceeds the limit of ballast release.

14:55.090 --> 14:56.390
Toraji!

14:59.160 --> 15:01.150
All hands, abandon ship!

15:02.830 --> 15:04.300
All hands abandon ship.

15:04.300 --> 15:07.130
Repeat: All hands abandon ship.

15:07.130 --> 15:11.140
After roll call, all departments shall quickly
board designated lifeboats.

15:11.140 --> 15:12.810
All hands abandon ship.

15:12.810 --> 15:15.440
Repeat: All hands abandon ship.

15:15.440 --> 15:15.780
After roll call, all departments...

15:15.780 --> 15:17.680
Oh crap... We're in trouble now...
After roll call, all departments...

15:17.680 --> 15:18.540
After roll call, all departments...

15:20.210 --> 15:21.980
Come on, get out. We're abandoning ship.

15:22.420 --> 15:23.920
The National Defense Force?

15:23.920 --> 15:26.080
Come on, hurry!

15:30.860 --> 15:32.590
Abandon ship?

15:40.730 --> 15:42.330
She got away?

15:43.670 --> 15:45.540
I let my guard down for a second and...

15:57.650 --> 15:59.480
That's one of the battleship's...

16:00.920 --> 16:02.220
Is it Renée?

16:03.060 --> 16:05.630
She's planning on escaping to the military?

16:05.630 --> 16:09.150
If she were that easy to read,
we wouldn't have any problems.

16:13.270 --> 16:16.530
Oh man, we're screwed now.

16:20.210 --> 16:22.730
Sana, let's get outta here.

16:24.550 --> 16:26.410
Sana! Let's go!

16:29.210 --> 16:30.340
NUMBER18
BULKHEAD

16:33.790 --> 16:35.120
This way.

16:45.570 --> 16:49.870
You don't need to ping to know
where the enemy is, do you?

16:50.240 --> 16:51.700
Toraji!

16:55.210 --> 16:59.110
Or, are you looking for a place to die, Oryo?

17:06.250 --> 17:10.780
Or maybe you're trying to act as a decoy
to divert attention away from the Ishin?

17:11.090 --> 17:13.790
Man, I'm so grateful, it makes me wanna cry.

17:14.060 --> 17:17.760
Didn't I tell you not to do anything stupid?

17:18.370 --> 17:20.330
You scumbag.

17:20.330 --> 17:24.000
I've never heard of a captain
abandoning his sinking ship.

17:24.640 --> 17:29.080
Well, you're looking at one.
I trust my subordinates, you know.

17:29.440 --> 17:32.150
Yeah, that all sounds great,

17:32.150 --> 17:34.910
but when you get down to it,
all you think about is running away.

17:35.850 --> 17:39.750
Don't you think I'm better off than someone
who frantically searches for a place to die

17:39.750 --> 17:42.090
because she no longer has a place to stay?

17:58.940 --> 18:01.010
Come off it!

18:01.010 --> 18:04.970
I can't stand the thought of you saving us
and making us feel indebted for your death.

18:05.680 --> 18:09.480
If you're gonna make me owe you one,
then lemme pay you back.

18:09.480 --> 18:12.710
I've owed you one for a long time now.

18:15.160 --> 18:18.790
Now that I'm here, I'll join you as a decoy.

18:18.790 --> 18:21.350
But I have no intentions of getting killed.

18:21.800 --> 18:23.820
What's your plan?

18:24.060 --> 18:28.020
The weapons on this ship won't do
much damage anyway.

18:28.470 --> 18:32.770
We'll cause a sonar disturbance, shoot
like crazy, then get the hell out.

18:33.140 --> 18:36.740
The radar will pick us up right away.
It'll be impossible to escape.

18:37.480 --> 18:40.150
DRFM will be used as the jammer.

18:40.150 --> 18:43.010
It delays the radar wave and then sends it back.

18:43.720 --> 18:48.210
Listen, now that I'm helping you here,
that'll settle part of my debt to you.

18:48.990 --> 18:53.060
But in return, give me a chance to
repay the rest to you, okay?

18:53.060 --> 18:56.030
What are you talking about?
You're not making any sense...

18:56.030 --> 18:57.620
Got that?

18:59.230 --> 19:02.460
Don't let go of my hand, Sana.

19:07.140 --> 19:11.840
Sana... This time, I'll be the one to...

19:14.850 --> 19:15.970
Joe...

19:27.130 --> 19:29.490
Are you okay, Joe?

19:39.210 --> 19:40.330
Joe...

19:51.850 --> 19:53.220
Hurry!

19:59.990 --> 20:01.860
Let's get outta here, Renée!

20:02.330 --> 20:03.460
Roger!

20:23.150 --> 20:24.780
The Ishin is...

20:46.240 --> 20:48.400
Looks like we made it.

20:53.210 --> 20:58.410
And as promised, I'll take my time
repaying the rest, Renée.

21:06.360 --> 21:09.660
Joe, that scar...

21:22.180 --> 21:23.140
Joe!

21:24.650 --> 21:26.240
I'm okay.

21:35.520 --> 21:38.920
You saved me back then...

21:45.600 --> 21:50.160
You really saved me back then...

22:25.170 --> 22:29.680
Nagai kioku no hate ni

22:25.170 --> 22:29.640
If at the end of our long memory

22:29.640 --> 22:35.480
Time will tear us apart

22:29.680 --> 22:35.510
Toki ga bokura o wakatsu nara

22:37.520 --> 22:44.160
If at the end of my sweet memory with you

22:37.550 --> 22:44.190
Kimi to amai kioku no hate ni

22:44.160 --> 22:50.460
You and I become one again

22:44.190 --> 22:50.500
Mata bokura hitotsu nara

22:50.460 --> 22:57.640
From a quietly stretched arm's length away

22:50.500 --> 22:57.670
Sotto te nobashita kyori kara

22:57.640 --> 23:02.340
I will search for the meaning

22:57.670 --> 23:02.380
lmi o sagasu kara

23:02.340 --> 23:08.180
Can you hear it? The words dance in midair

23:02.380 --> 23:08.220
Kikoeru? Kotoba ga chuu ni mau

23:08.180 --> 23:13.990
We shall meet when our wish is granted

23:08.220 --> 23:14.020
Kanaeta toki ni deau

23:13.990 --> 23:17.660
Leaving only their reverse behind

23:14.020 --> 23:17.690
Reverse dake nokoshite

23:17.660 --> 23:21.060
The torn words

23:17.690 --> 23:21.090
Chigireta kotoba

23:21.060 --> 23:27.190
Blurred time and light

23:21.090 --> 23:27.230
Kasureta jikan to hikari

23:29.370 --> 23:33.700
I have found them now

23:29.400 --> 23:33.740
lma, mitsuketa kara

23:35.230 --> 23:46.320
<b><i>Next Episode</i></b>

23:44.350 --> 23:47.240
Next time on Innocent Venus:

23:47.530 --> 23:50.650
Episode 10
Determination

23:47.790 --> 23:49.460
"Determination"
